    {
      "s": "TechCrunch",
      "t": "OpenAI makes its Jev competitor widely available as decision model competition heats up",
      "d": "OpenAI is launching its decision model to the world. Can it compete with the original Jev?",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/22/openai-makes-its-jev-competitor-widely-available-as-decision-model-competition-heats-up/",
      "m": "10. 22. PM 07:00",
      "ts": 1792695600000,
      "fullText": "OpenAI made its Decisions API model widely available to users for the first time, entering the market for fast, cheap intelligence that recently made TypeSafe, a startup founded by a former researcher at the frontier lab, a $7.6 billion company . TypeSafe&#8217;s Jev model created a category for deep learning models that act as super classifiers: Given a set of options, they can quickly make choices and offer a confidence rating in their decision. Software developers quickly found that these decision or System One models could replace LLMs in a variety of workflows, operating more quickly and a at dramatically lower cost. Nikunj Handa, the product lead for OpenAI&#8217;s APIs, told TechCrunch that his colleagues saw Jev and said &#8220;wow, we we have like a million use cases for this.&#8221; Handa&#8217;s team sprinted to offer their own version: Rather than building a specifically calibrated decision model, the team took ChatGPT Luna and reconfigured it to speed up the inference and lower the cost. &#8220;The big unlock with Decisions API has been the speed, shrinking things from one to three seconds to 100, 120, 180 milliseconds,&#8221; Handa said. &#8220;In the future, we may sort of like have specific training to make our models like even better in these ways. But right now, it&#8217;s just plain old Luna that gets the job done.&#8221; Announced at the company&#8217;s developer day on September 29, the Decisions API became available to all customers on Thursday. OpenAI added new voice and visual modalities to the public version, and worked to ensure lower latency in regions around the world by targeting its inference resources geographically. In initial trials with customers like Box, Datadog, Ramp, and Speak, engineers used the API to replace OpenAI&#8217;s LLMs with higher throughput. Andrew Hsu, the CTO at Speak, which builds AI language tutors, said the Decisions API allowed the company to cut the time between actions from 1.4 seconds to .13 seconds. OpenAI"
    },
